					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><strong>« <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-10-2020">October 2020</a> | <span style="text-decoration: underline;"><a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-11-2020">November 2020</a></span> | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/news-12-2020">December 2020</a> »</strong></p> </div> <p><span style="font-size:75%;">This is a series showing off news from the site, articles from the past month<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-706668-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>, and fan-content for you to check out and discover! Be sure to leave a comment with your thoughts!</span></p> <h4><span>Fandom Stuff</span></h4> <ul> <li>SCP-FR (French language branch of the SCP Foundation) is running <a href="http://fondationscp.wikidot.com/le-concours-des-404-ans">a contest</a> for the SCP-404-FR slot. Participants are asked to write about &quot;An error, something that caused one or the consequences of one&quot;. The visual design of the contest hub is worth checking out whether you speak French or not.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-EN (English, this wiki) is conducting another <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/instagram-fan-art-contest-fall-2020">Instagram Fan Art Contest</a>.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-PL (Polish) is running the inventive <a href="http://scp-pl.wikidot.com/rezurekcja-usunietych">Resurrecting The Deleted</a> contest. Participants pick a title of a work from the Deletions Log, and write an article using said title.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-KO (Korean) finished its latest <a href="http://ko.scp-wiki.net/bimonthly-contests-2020#toc4">bimonthly contest</a>. The theme of the contest was &quot;Language&quot;.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-DE (German) concluded its second <a href="http://scp-wiki-de.wikidot.com/halloween-wettbewerb-2020">Halloween contest</a>.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-IT (Italian) also ran a <a href="http://fondazionescp.wikidot.com/concorso-halloween-2020-dr-zeno">Halloween contest</a> this month.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Featured Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5380">SCP-5380</a> (by chiifu): My World [Featured by Truc Linh and Quadraginta]<br /> <em>As a result, the entire mall was showered with snowflakes and small paper hearts.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-significant-others-part-a">The Significant Others, Part &quot;A&quot;</a> by HarryBlank [Featured by weizhong, Grigori Karpin, and PlaguePJP]<br /> <em>&quot;I'm not a subject in containment,&quot; said Phil.</em><br /> <em>Azad grinned. &quot;Sure you're not.&quot;</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/deer-and-the-overseers">Deer And The Overseers</a> <tt>[Deer College]</tt> by stormbreath [Featured by The Pighead, Marcelles_Raynes, and Pedagon]<br /> <em>In honor of the termination of the old Council, I'll be looking at the history of Deer's interactions with them…</em></li> </ul> <h4><span>Reviewer's Spotlight Articles</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5462">SCP-5462</a> (Misery is the State of Every Soul Burdened by Mortality.) by Cerastes [Selected by Cerastes]<br /> <em>[…] commonly referred to as his Black Paintings due to their emotionally disturbing contents, themes, and use of dark colours.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5456">SCP-5456</a> (Sweatmother) by faminepulse [Selected by Grigori Karpin]<br /> <em>“We can be human, yeah we can be respectful, but we can't tolerate chaos. You</em> have <em>to be our<sup>[sic]</sup> own dads.”</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4423">SCP-4423</a> (StepDemon) by Dyslexion [Selected by Sonderance]<br /> <em>SCP-4423 is a Tartarean-Class demonic entity that manifests during sleep paralysis.</em></li> </ul> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5788">SCP-5788</a> (Partners in sync) by Riemann [Selected by OCuin]<br /> <em>The integration of SCP-5788 into the plumbing of the kitchen makes removal and characterisation difficult.</em></li> </ul> <div id="toc" class="floatright"> <div id="toc-action-bar"><a href="javascript:;" >Fold</a><a style="display: none" href="javascript:;" >Unfold</a></div> <div class="title">Table of Contents</div> <div id="toc-list"> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc0">Week of November 1st:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc1">Week of November 8th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc2">Week of November 15th:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 4em;"><a href="#toc3">*GoI Formats</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc4">Week of November 22nd:</a></div> <div style="margin-left: 3em;"><a href="#toc5">Fanart</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p>You will notice little '📈' emojis beside some articles. That denotes SCP articles which were under 30 and tales which were under 20 when this edition of site news was posted. Give them a little love! Speaking from personal experience, the most frustrating thing that can happen to an article is not deletion, but stagnating below 20 without any comments. So try to read, vote, and comment on these articles! They're often hidden gems :)</p> <h3><span>Week of November 1st:</span></h3> <h4><span>SCPs</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5178">SCP-5178</a> (&quot;Eat The Sun with Seth Uhar&quot;) - And for today's recipe, we will learn how to incorporate little bits of sun into your homemade Margharita pizza. Cooked and brought to you by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decoymesa" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4733271&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="DecoyMesa" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4733271)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decoymesa" >DecoyMesa</a></span>.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5733">SCP-5733</a> (&quot;Knife. Scream. Cut to Black.&quot;) - Ordinary. Death. No. Remembrance. <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dysadron" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4384469&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="Dysadron" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4384469)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dysadron" >Dysadron</a></span>. Writer.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5414">SCP-5414</a> (&quot;Clouds Only Dreamt&quot;) - And if humans can dream, maybe it means we're clouds too. Written by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barbarous-bread" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6880816&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="Barbarous Bread" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6880816)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/barbarous-bread" >Barbarous Bread</a></span>.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5170">SCP-5170</a> (&quot;<strong>Pattern Screamer, Esq.</strong> 💼⚖️&quot;) - Because these days, we need to put emojis everywhere. It gives you a more friendly image. Written by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/amytato" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3168871&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="Amytato" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3168871)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/amytato" >Amytato</a></span>.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5598">SCP-5598</a> (&quot;I, Eurydice Ferlinghetti&quot;) - I'm still waiting for my Orpheus. Written by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lordstonefish" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2527320&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="LordStonefish" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2527320)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lordstonefish" >LordStonefish</a></span>.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5146">SCP-5146</a> (&quot;Perfect Territory&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/daviiid" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6403884&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="daviiid" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6403884)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/daviiid" >daviiid</a></span>.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5132">SCP-5132</a> (&quot;The Kids Aren't Alright&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raddagher" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5364476&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="Raddagher" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5364476)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raddagher" >Raddagher</a></span>.</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5957">SCP-5957</a> (&quot;A Baleful Light&quot;) - &quot;blurb&quot; Written by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264907" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" >Grigori Karpin</a></span>.</li> </ul> <h4><span>Tales</span></h4> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/eating-honey-in-the-rain">Eating Honey in the Rain</a> - &quot;<em>Oh, how gentle the fruit is from the Moon's sweet carcass, as if harvested from the giant maw of a bee stung beas