						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5672</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe/Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5672-A, SCP-5672-B, and SCP-5672-C are to be kept in three (3) separate standard humanoid containment cells at Site-██, adjacent to each other and accessible by level two (2) clearance or higher. Tesla gates are stationed outside each cell and are to be kept online indefinitely.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5672-A, SCP-5672-B and SCP-5672-C are the skeletons of humans, each being around 6'2&quot; and weighing 27 pounds average. They were found in a cave in █████, England. They were found in a large pool of liquid, found to be a mix of water with several minerals in, and strange glue like green substance. This might be the reason for their perfect preservation, or their anomalous abilities. No one knows if the skeletons were once living organisms, or if they were formed as a pile of bones. All anomaly's have 206 bones and 32 perfect teeth. All bones are a clear white colour, and made of collagen and calcium phosphate, the normal composition for the bones of a healthy adult. However, it has been tested that these anomalous entities are indestructible, being resistant to hydrofluoric acid, over 5,000°C and over 900,500 pascals of pressure. The bones and the invisible couplings for them appear to be indestructible, or at least to the point of human technology. The only way the foundation has proven to dismantle SCP-5672 is through 3000v of electricity. This voltage breaks the strength between the bones and they fall into a pile on the ground. This usually takes 1-2 hours to recover from.</p> <p>SCP-5672-A through SCP-5672-C all have different anomalous abilities, however none have used them against the facility so far. The abilities have a limit to what they can do, and have a limit on how much they can use their abilities.</p> <ul> <li>SCP-5672-A can conjure any item ranging from 1-6000g out of nowhere. This seems to tire SCP-5672-A if used repeatedly, but it enjoys giving these items to facility staff. No negative items have been produced yet. When asked to produce dangerous items such as a gun or a small bomb, it kindly declined.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>SCP-5672-B has the ability to teleport in a range of 3 metres. It mostly uses this for its own good.</li> </ul> <p>It can teleport around its containment cell, but has moved out of its cell once, see Addendum-5672-B1. This drains its stamina, strength and integrity if used repeatedly.</p> <ul> <li>SCP-5672-C can read the brainwave patterns of nearby humans. This ability can duplicate the brainwaves of someone into the anomaly. This function is inhibited by lead, therefore its containment cell is surrounded in 5cm of lead coating to prevent the spread of information. It is not currently known if it can add/change brainwaves in beings.</li> </ul> <p>SCP-5672-A, SCP-5672-B and SCP-5672-C have the ability to talk, despite having a lack of a voice box and/or lungs. All 3 anomaly's have higher brain functions, scoring 98% on intelligence tests. All variations of SCP-5672 are friendly unless provoked, asking for the person who angered it to, &quot;Kindly back away.&quot; In most severe confrontations, SCP-5672-C has attacked the Class-D who angered it, and ████████, killing them instantly. This seems to be a last resort maybe to preserve its kind, or to might be down to its passive nature. SCP-5672 and its iterations are polite and cordial to research staff and have been quoted to be enjoyable to work with. SCP-5672 and its companions willingly entered containment, asking guards if they would like a beverage or any delicacies on hand to SCP-5672-A. Ongoing tests are seeing if their nature is polite, or if they are just being nice to staff.</p> <p><strong>Addendum-5672-B1:</strong> During testing of SCP-5672-B, the entity teleported outside of its containment cell. It teleported into a nearby observation room, but only half of it emerged in the floor, the other half, its pelvis, femur, tibia and fibula had been stuck in the concrete floor, until shifted again, this time back into its cell.</p> <p><strong>Addendum-5672-1:</strong> If an entity uses it anomalous abilities too much, it will get &quot;tired&quot; and sit motionless for 2-4 hours. If continued use of their abilities occurs, the couplings that hold their structure together will snap, causing the bones to fall onto the floor into a pile, as if you removed the skeleton from a skeleton. after 3-6 hours of being a pile of bones, SCP-5672 will reform itself into is normal shape. This has happened twice.</p> <p>A DNA test and carbon-dating tests were conducted on the bones of SCP-5672-A. Carbon dating suggests the bones came from the 15th century. DNA tests shocked researchers when remaining genes, alleles and genetics were closely similar to the ones of King Henry VIII. Caesium-135 and Strontium-99 found in minute traces suggest exposure to radioactive material. No known nuclear bomb/accident has ever occurred in the United Kingdom.</p> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-xxxw">SCP-XXXW</a> | SCP-5672| <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-xxxy">SCP-XXXY</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-cheese" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6525339&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607264913" alt="Doctor Cheese" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6525339)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-cheese" >Doctor Cheese</a></span></p> 
